// Building the Satsuma the way My Summer Car does it, with nobody at the keys: the left door, the front left wheel and
// the radiator each picked up by MSC's own hand (`fetch <part> eyes` holds the part under the crosshair, a left click
// picks it up), held to its place on the body (`offer <trigger>`: its Assembly FSM counts the part as come in, MSC checks
// the hand and shows its assemble icon, which has to reach Skyrim), clicked on, bolted with MSC's wrench (2 for the tools,
// the size from MSC's own spanner set by the car's nose (`open` opens its lid, as the use key does; lying down, `spanner`
// stands Kumpo at the spanner that fits the part's bolts and a left click takes it: MSC's 2Spanner/Pick), `look ... BoltPM #n`
// aims at each bolt, crouched or lying down to reach it, and `pr.wheel 14` turns it all the way in: eight stages, notches
// spare for the ones MSC drops in the pause between its stages; every bolt twice round, as the aim can drift off a nut
// mid-turn and an extra turn on a tight bolt does nothing), unbolted (`pr.wheel -14`) and, the door and the radiator, taken off
// again with a right click on MSC's disassemble icon. MSC's own state is checked at each step through the probe
// (`pr.part`: MSC's database as Skyrim got it, and whether Skyrim draws the part on the car), and both games are
// pictured: Skyrim with `screenshot`, MSC's own view with `pr.mscshot` (Documents/My Games/PerkeleRim/Screenshots).
// The Satsuma stands in its bay on its stand (the session's handover moves it there, `pr.garage`), every part off
// (`bare`), its body held still (`freeze`, again after each part, as MSC's own assembly lets the car go). A bare test car has no suspension under the
// front left corner, so the wheel's setup marks its disc brake fitted in MSC's database (`fsmvar`, the session never
// saves). The wheel stays on: MSC takes one off only while it is off the ground (its Removal checks the wheel's
// OnGroundDown), and on this stripped car, even resting free on the stand, MSC still has it touching the floor. The radiator's other three bolts sit too deep for the
// scenario's aim; MSC counts it bolted from its first (BoltedYES 2). Runs from a session's start (Kumpo standing).
// scripts/skytest.ps1 run scenarios/satsuma-bolting.json in a running session; MSC's lines (`cmd: fetch:`, `cmd: offer:`,
// `cmd: look:`, `cmd: wrench:`, `cmd: aim: a second on ...`) are in its PerkeleRim_spike.log, `parts:` in output_log.txt
// and PerkeleRim.log.
{
  "name": "satsuma-bolting",
  "steps": [
    {"label": "MSC has Kumpo", "cmd": "pr.msc", "expect": ["msc == true"]},
